---
// Snow and ice in Mon County (#1005): who clears which roads, the city's
// sidewalk rule, school closings and late buses. Alerts, road conditions and
// power outage texts are on /weather-alerts/. Wave 11 (#529) added buses in
// winter weather, getting a home and car ready, water pipes and power.
// Not here yet: rules for Westover, Star City and Granville, a snow-specific
// way to report a state road, a Morgantown rule on parking during snow, and
// frozen pipe advice from MUB (none found on an official page we can read).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import BigChoices from '../components/BigChoices.astro';
import OnThisPage from '../components/OnThisPage.astro';
import ResourceCard from '../components/ResourceCard.astro';
import SourceLine from '../components/SourceLine.astro';
import { loadDir, telHref } from '../lib/content.mjs';
import { fixFormUrl } from '../lib/group-requests.mjs';
export const page = { door: "living-here", topic: "weather", label: "Snow and ice: who plows, sidewalks, schools and buses", summary: "Which roads get cleared first, the 24-hour sidewalk rule in Morgantown, school closings and late buses" };
const all = loadDir('resources');
const r = (slug) => all.find((e) => e.slug === slug);
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const checked = '2026-11-02';
const src = {
  busWinter: [{ url: 'https://www.busride.org/winter-weather-notice', checked, name: 'Mountain Line winter weather notice, January 23, 2026' }],
  ready: [{ url: 'https://www.monchd.org/newsroom/winterizing-goes-a-long-way-toward-staying-safe', checked, name: 'Monongalia County Health Department, January 14, 2026' }],
  pipes: [
    { url: 'https://mub.org/', checked, name: 'Morgantown Utility Board' },
    { url: 'https://www.ready.gov/winter-weather', checked, name: 'Ready.gov winter weather' },
  ],
};
const outage = r('mon-power-report-outage');
---
<Base title="Snow and ice in Morgantown and Mon County: plowing, sidewalks, schools" description="Who clears snow from city streets and state roads in Morgantown and Monongalia County, which roads go first, the 24-hour sidewalk rule, where school closings are posted, and how to see if your bus is late.">
  <h1>Snow and ice in Mon County</h1>
  <p class="lede">Who clears a road depends on who owns it. In Morgantown, the city clears city streets. The state clears state roads. Both start with the busiest roads, so side streets come last.</p>
  {/* Lead block (#199): the four things most people come here for on a snowy morning. */}
  <BigChoices label="Snow and ice: start here" choices={[
    { href: '#city', label: 'Morgantown street or sidewalk', icon: 'home' },
    { href: '#state', label: 'State road', icon: 'pin' },
    { href: '#schools', label: 'School delays and closings', icon: 'calendar' },
    { href: '#buses', label: 'Is my bus late?', icon: 'clock' },
  ]} />
  <OnThisPage items={[['#ready', 'Get your home and car ready'], ['#pipes', 'Water pipes'], ['#power', 'Power out'], ['#alerts', 'Alerts and road conditions']]} />

  <h2 id="city">City of Morgantown streets and sidewalks</h2>
  {r('morgantown-snow-plan') && <ResourceCard r={r('morgantown-snow-plan')} />}

  <h2 id="state">State roads</h2>
  {r('wvdoh-snow-priorities') && <ResourceCard r={r('wvdoh-snow-priorities')} />}
  <p>Not sure if a road is a state road? Use the state's <a href="https://experience.arcgis.com/experience/2917da07ad1d4900bb4e372ca6527126/page/Page">road search by address</a> map.</p>

  <h2 id="schools">School delays and closings</h2>
  {r('mcs-school-closings') && <ResourceCard r={r('mcs-school-closings')} />}

  <h2 id="buses">Buses</h2>
  {r('mountain-line-ticker') && <ResourceCard r={r('mountain-line-ticker')} />}
  <p>In winter weather, Mountain Line says local routes keep running as long as roads allow. When a road can't be driven, it posts the change right away on its ticker on X, <a href="https://x.com/MLticker">@MLticker</a>. The Grey Line to Pittsburgh can stop running when Pennsylvania closes roads. <SourceLine sources={src.busWinter} about="buses in winter weather" /></p>

  <h2 id="ready">Get your home and car ready</h2>
  <p>The Monongalia County Health Department gives these winter tips:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Heaters:</strong> keep at least 3 feet of space around fireplaces and space heaters. Do not plug a space heater into a power strip, keep it away from fabric, and do not leave it on when no one is there.</li>
    <li><strong>Detectors:</strong> check the batteries in your smoke and carbon monoxide detectors.</li>
    <li><strong>Generators:</strong> never run one inside. If you use a portable generator, you need a working carbon monoxide detector.</li>
    <li><strong>Home kit:</strong> keep at least 3 days of supplies for each person and pet, including a gallon of water a day for each person, food that won't spoil, a can opener, a battery radio, flashlights and a phone charger.</li>
    <li><strong>Car kit:</strong> blankets, snacks, jumper cables, a phone charger, a flashlight, a first aid kit, and sand or cat litter to help tires grip. Keep your gas tank on the fuller side.</li>
    <li><strong>Shoveling:</strong> stretch first and go slow. Push snow instead of lifting it. If you lift, fill the shovel only part way and lift with your legs. Take breaks.</li>
  </ul>
  <SourceLine sources={src.ready} about="winter tips" />
  <p>Need help paying for heat? See <a href={`${base}/utility-bills/`}>Help paying a utility bill</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="pipes">Water pipes</h2>
  <p>For a water emergency, like a broken water main or no water, call the Morgantown Utility Board (MUB) at <a href={telHref('304-292-8443')}>304-292-8443</a>. MUB says the line answers emergencies 24 hours a day. MUB's website does not give tips on frozen pipes. Ready.gov, the federal emergency site, links to <a href="https://www.ready.gov/winter-weather">tips to keep pipes from freezing</a>.</p>
  <SourceLine sources={src.pipes} about="water emergencies and frozen pipes" />

  {outage && <>
    <h2 id="power">Power out</h2>
    <p>Report it to Mon Power at <a href={telHref(outage.contact.phone)}>{outage.contact.phone}</a>, or text OUT to 544487 after you sign up by texting REG. More on what to do is on <a href={`${base}/after-a-storm/#power`}>Storm damage, flooding or power out?</a></p>
    <SourceLine sources={outage.sources} org={outage.org} about="reporting an outage" slug={outage.slug} />
  </>}

  <h2 id="alerts">Alerts and road conditions</h2>
  <p>Weather warnings, WV 511 road conditions and Mon Power outage texts are on <a href={`${base}/weather-alerts/`}>Get weather and emergency alerts</a>.</p>

  <p class="meta">Each section shows when we last checked its source. Westover, Star City and Granville do not post snow rules on their websites; call your town hall to ask. We have not found a Morgantown rule about parking on the street during snow on a city page we can read. Something out of date? <a href={fixFormUrl({ page: Astro.url.pathname })}>Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>
